contentText:
Hayley Williams isn&#8217;t backing down on her beliefs.

The Paramore frontwoman had a simple message for the Department of Homeland Security after she shouted &#8220;F&#8211;k ICE&#8221; and &#8220;Free Palestine&#8221; during her recent concert in Chula Vista, California. DHS responded to the singer&#8217;s remarks through a statement to Fox News, saying that Americans should be grateful for federal law enforcement officers and suggesting that the singer &#8220;thank them for their service, not belittle their sacrifice.&#8221;

Williams shared the department&#8217;s statement to her Instagram Story on Monday (Oct. 5), adding her own decidedly less diplomatic response. &#8220;And may I suggest all Nazi bi&#8212;es suck on my fat di&#8211;,&#8221; Williams wrote.

